      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In general I totally agree with this. People keep complaining about the state of moderation in public worlds, and VRChat keep telling us it's up to us to moderate our own experience. Better tools to do so are absolutely needed and this idea is in the right direction.\nOne major problem I see is that a permanent world ban opens up some odd issues. What if Owlboy banned me from The Great Pug, but some friends of mine had a private party there? I don't think I should be blocked from going there in that case.\nPublic world ban, yes. Private, no.\nThis would also serve as another useful flag for VRC's moderation team. If a person just keeps getting banned from worlds, there's clearly something to pay attention to here. Especially if all the users who hand out the ban have no connection to each other.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
